<section class="section" aria-labelledby="coming-title">
	<h2 id="coming-title">Coming from another language?</h2>
	<p class="intro">Each guide puts the same program side by side in your language and in Burdin.</p>
	<ul class="langs">
		<li>
			<a href="/coming-from/rust/">
				<span class="name">Rust</span>
				<span class="note">Ownership without lifetime annotations, and the Option and Result you already know.</span>
			</a>
		</li>
		<li>
			<a href="/coming-from/go/">
				<span class="name">Go</span>
				<span class="note">Small structs and interfaces, with errors as values and no collector.</span>
			</a>
		</li>
		<li>
			<a href="/coming-from/python/">
				<span class="name">Python</span>
				<span class="note">Interpolated strings and for loops, with every type checked before the program runs.</span>
			</a>
		</li>
		<li>
			<a href="/coming-from/c-and-cpp/">
				<span class="name">C and C++</span>
				<span class="note">Value semantics, destructors as Drop, and no raw pointers in ordinary code.</span>
			</a>
		</li>
	</ul>
</section>

